    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_3adc1785a285ac3f057a23a0d2b688cf05a03b47c74a0450b1be0288c445b1ad",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The two large-value estimates support a regime-dependent choice rather than a global ranking: the paper's estimate is sharper when V is large and leads to gains near four-fifths, whereas Huxley's estimate is better near three-quarters. This gives a qualitative selection rule but no safe exact crossover, exponent, or threshold; those quantitative proof obligations remain with the original scan.",
