    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_4a48cea3e8820f1732221074eb6d8532243f816ff4c34c94f520258578d08c53",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Contour motion and the functional equation reorganize the original expression into a controlled finite dual partial sum and a remainder handled by separate contour moves, yielding a qualitative main-term/error split. The primitive-character case supplies the basic representation; the imprimitive case requires extra inserted factors. The gain is this decomposition into tractable roles, while exact lengths, factors, and error sizes remain unverified.",
