    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_68a9be9600b6ad0e9c3e15179236453664ecaefeede7f0ea3cc2ef4e2383ec13",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Discrete fourth-moment estimates provide collective control across the separated points and characters in the two stated character-family cases. The proof changes treatment with the length regime, using a direct fourth-moment estimate or an integral representation, while Ramachandra's alternative avoids difficulties associated with the approximate functional equation. This gains family-level control from moment information, but the OCR does not preserve the exact bounds, ranges, moduli, or powers.",
